steps.prompt:
GROUP BY splits rows into piles that share something.
'How many products live in each category?' - each category becomes one pile, and count(*) counts the pile.
SELECT category_id, count(*) FROM products GROUP BY ___;

Someone forgot the rules of piles:
SELECT category_id, count(*) FROM products;
The database complains: mixing per-row values with the grand total is confusing.

Each pile from GROUP BY can be turned back into a name with a JOIN:
SELECT c.name, count(*) AS n FROM products p JOIN categories c ON p.category_id = c.id GROUP BY c.name;
The pile with the highest count holds the most products.
